{"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftllm\/metalshadersquantization"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedTensor","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLayoutMetadata","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLinear","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizationScheme","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedEngine","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedError"],"anchor":"Quantization--Metal-Execution","title":"Quantization & Metal Execution"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftLLM"}],"title":"Native Metal MSL Shaders for Quantized LLMs","roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hardware dequantization and SIMD-group matrix multiplication for 4-bit and 8-bit quantized weights on Apple Silicon GPU."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalShadersQuantization"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderArchitecture","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderInference","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SamplingAndDecodingStrategies","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/WeightParsingAndSampling"],"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","title":"Guides & Tutorials","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Large language models like Llama 3, Mistral, and DeepSeek require massive memory bandwidth. Weight-only quantization (such as GGUF Q4_0 and Q8_0) compresses 16-bit floating-point weights into 4-bit or 8-bit integer blocks with group scaling factors, reducing memory footprint by 50% to 75%.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftLLM","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" implements native Metal Shading Language (MSL) SIMD kernels executing hardware dequantization and GEMV \/ GEMM transformations directly on Apple Silicon GPUs without intermediate CPU memory allocations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Architecture","anchor":"Architecture"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["Packed Quantized Weights [Q4_0 \/ Q8_0]   Scale Factors [FP16]   Input Activations [FP32]","                 │                               │                        │","                 └───────────────────────┬───────┴────────────────────────┘","                                         ▼","                   Metal Compute Command Encoder","                                         │","                 ┌───────────────────────┴───────────────────────┐","                 ▼                                               ▼","     MSL Kernel: gemv_q4_0                           MSL Kernel: gemv_q8_0","   - Unpack 4-bit nibbles (w - 8)                  - Load signed 8-bit integers","   - Multiply by group FP16 scale                  - Multiply by group FP16 scale","   - Accumulate with input vector                  - Accumulate with input vector","                 │                                               │","                 └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘","                                         ▼","                            Output Activation Vector","                               (Unified Memory)"],"syntax":null},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"SIMD-Group Matrix Multiplication","anchor":"SIMD-Group-Matrix-Multiplication"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On Apple Silicon (M-series GPUs), threads within a 32-thread SIMD-group collaborate on 8x8 matrix tiles using ","type":"text"},{"code":"metal_simdgroup_matrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This eliminates thread divergence and ensures maximal utilization of the GPU arithmetic units:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["#include <metal_stdlib>","#include <metal_simdgroup_matrix>","","using namespace metal;","","kernel void gemm_simdgroup_q4_0(","    device const half* A               [[buffer(0)]],","    device const half* B               [[buffer(1)]],","    device half* C                     [[buffer(2)]],","    constant uint& M                   [[buffer(3)]],","    constant uint& N                   [[buffer(4)]],","    constant uint& K                   [[buffer(5)]],","    uint2 threadgroup_position_in_grid [[threadgroup_position_in_grid]],","    uint simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup [[simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup]]",") {","    simdgroup_matrix<half, 8, 8> acc;","    acc = make_filled_simdgroup_matrix<half, 8, 8>(0.0h);","    \/\/ Accumulate across inner K dimension...","}"],"syntax":"metal"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Swift API Integration: From QuantizedTensor to Metal GEMV","anchor":"Swift-API-Integration-From-QuantizedTensor-to-Metal-GEMV"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftLLM","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" unifies parsed weight storage and GPU execution through a zero-copy pipeline:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"$$\\text{GGUF File} \\xrightarrow{\\text{GGUFParser}} \\text{QuantizedTensor} \\xrightarrow{\\text{extractSeparatedBuffers}} \\text{QuantizedLinear.forwardMetal} \\xrightarrow{\\text{MSL SIMD}} \\text{Output Activation}$$","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"1. Extracting Separated Buffers from QuantizedTensor","anchor":"1-Extracting-Separated-Buffers-from-QuantizedTensor"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"QuantizedTensor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" preserves the raw binary layout (e.g. 18-byte Q4_0 blocks) with ","type":"text"},{"code":"QuantizedLayoutMetadata","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", allowing separation of packed weights and scale factors:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Foundation","import SwiftLLM","","\/\/ 1. Load tensor from parsed GGUF dictionary","guard let tensor = parsedWeights[\"blk.0.attn_q.weight\"],","      let buffers = tensor.extractSeparatedBuffers() else {","    fatalError(\"Failed to extract quantized buffers\")","}","","let packedWeights: Data = buffers.weights","let packedScales: Data = buffers.scales"],"syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"2. Direct Metal Kernel Execution via QuantizedLinear","anchor":"2-Direct-Metal-Kernel-Execution-via-QuantizedLinear"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"QuantizedLinear","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" encapsulates both MLX-accelerated layer evaluations and native Metal MSL shader execution (","type":"text"},{"code":"gemv_q4_0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"gemv_q8_0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ 2. Initialize layer geometry and scheme","let linear = QuantizedLinear(","    inFeatures: 4096,","    outFeatures: 4096,","    scheme: .q4_0,","    weight: tensor.dequantizeToFloat(), \/\/ MLXArray fallback\/graph evaluation","    scales: MLXArray(0.0)",")","","\/\/ 3. Direct Metal GEMV execution without CPU round-trips or allocations","let outputActivations: [Float] = try linear.forwardMetal(","    inVector: inputActivations,","    rawWeights: packedWeights,","    rawScalesData: packedScales",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forwardMetal"},{"type":"text","text":" runs packed Q4_0\/Q8_0 Metal MSL kernels directly on packed bytes. Invoking "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"QuantizedLinear"},{"type":"text","text":" via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"callAsFunction"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TransformerDecoder.loadWeights(_: [String: QuantizedTensor])"},{"type":"text","text":" executes the Float32 "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLXArray"},{"type":"text","text":" dequantized fallback; full-model packed 4-bit\/8-bit execution in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TransformerDecoder"},{"type":"text","text":" uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWeights(_: [String: MLXArray])"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadQuantizedWeights(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" backed by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLXNN.QuantizedLinear"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/SamplingAndDecodingStrategies":{"title":"Token Sampling & Decoding Strategies","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Control autoregressive language generation with Temperature, Top-P Nucleus, Top-K, and Repetition Penalty."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SamplingAndDecodingStrategies","url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/samplinganddecodingstrategies","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/QuantizationScheme":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"QuantizationScheme"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/quantizationscheme","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The quantization scheme used for compressed model weights.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizationScheme","role":"symbol","title":"QuantizationScheme","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"QuantizationScheme"}]},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/QuantizedLinear":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLinear","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"QuantizedLinear","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/quantizedlinear","title":"QuantizedLinear","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A linear neural network layer performing matrix multiplication with 4-bit (Q4_0, Q4_K) or 8-bit quantized weights."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"QuantizedLinear","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/MetalQuantizedEngine":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedEngine","title":"MetalQuantizedEngine","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A thread-safe executor and pipeline cache for Metal quantized MSL GEMV \/ GEMM kernels."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MetalQuantizedEngine"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MetalQuantizedEngine","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/metalquantizedengine"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/MetalQuantizedError":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MetalQuantizedError"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/metalquantizederror","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Errors occurring during Metal quantized kernel pipeline creation or GPU buffer execution.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedError","role":"symbol","title":"MetalQuantizedError","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MetalQuantizedError"}]},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/TransformerDecoderInference":{"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/transformerdecoderinference","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderInference","title":"Autoregressive Transformer Decoder Inference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Execute two-stage autoregressive generation with full prompt prefill and incremental single-token decoding using Apple Silicon KV-caching."}]},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/TransformerDecoderArchitecture":{"kind":"article","url":"